<BaseLayout title="Terms of Service" description="Terms for the Flowmaster website, accounts and online services: free and commercial use, your recordings, AI features, the desktop EULA, California law and support.">
  <article class="terms-page">
    <header>
      <p class="terms-label">FLOWMASTER · TERMS</p>
      <h1>Terms of Service</h1>
      <p class="terms-intro">These terms cover Flowmaster’s website, accounts and related online services. Flowmaster is provided by Alexander Blair, doing business as Flowmaster (“Flowmaster,” “we,” “us,” “our”).</p>
      <p class="terms-date">Effective November 24, 2026 · Last updated November 24, 2026</p>
    </header>
    <div class="terms-summary"><strong>The essentials</strong><p>Your recordings remain yours, and you may use Flowmaster for personal or commercial work, including content you publish or earn money from. Flowmaster’s recording, marking, clipping and clean-up features are free with a verified account. Cloud AI features send the material a task needs to AI providers, and AI output can be wrong. The desktop app’s own licence (EULA) governs the installed app; these terms govern the website and your account. California law applies.</p></div>

    <section aria-labelledby="scope"><h2 id="scope">1. These terms and the desktop licence</h2><p>These terms apply to flowmaster.live, your Flowmaster account, and Flowmaster’s online services, such as sign-in, licence and trial checks, update checks and AI features (the “Services”). If you do not agree, do not create an account or use the Services.</p><p>The Flowmaster desktop app is licensed under the <strong>Flowmaster Desktop App End User License Agreement and Terms of Use</strong> (the “EULA”), which you accept in the installer and which is included in the app’s installation folder (you can also ask us for a copy). The two documents fit together this way:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>For installing and using the desktop app, including its AI features, licence keys and trials as they operate in the app, the EULA controls. If the EULA and these terms conflict about the app, the EULA controls.</li>
        <li>For the website and your account, these terms control.</li>
        <li>If you buy a paid plan, the specific terms shown to you at purchase (such as price, billing period, renewal and cancellation) control for that purchase.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>Our <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a> explains how both the app and the Services handle information. Third-party and open-source components remain governed by their own licences and notices, and nothing here restricts rights that applicable law or those licences give you.</p></section>

    <section aria-labelledby="account"><h2 id="account">2. Your account</h2><p>Use an email address and sign-in account you control, provide accurate account information, and protect your password and sign-in credentials. Do not share or transfer access to bypass trial or licence restrictions. Tell us promptly if you believe someone has accessed your account without permission. You are responsible for activity under your account that you allow or that results from your failure to protect your sign-in details.</p><p>You must be able to enter a binding agreement under the law that applies to you, and Flowmaster is not for children under 13. If you use Flowmaster for an organization, you must have authority to act for it. Google sign-in is optional and does not grant administrator privileges or a paid licence.</p></section>

    <section aria-labelledby="trial"><h2 id="trial">3. Free use, commercial use and licences</h2><p>Flowmaster&rsquo;s recording, marking, clipping, clean-up and project assembly features are free to use, with no action limit and no scheduled time expiry. A verified free account and an internet connection are required to sign in and to start new work.</p><p><strong>Commercial use is allowed.</strong> You may use Flowmaster, including its free features, for personal or business purposes, including to create content that you publish, distribute or monetize. Labels such as “beta” or “preview” mean a build or feature may be incomplete or may change; they do not restrict commercial use. You may not resell, redistribute or offer Flowmaster itself as a service, as the EULA explains.</p><p>Existing recordings and outputs remain yours. Online sign-in and service availability can still affect access; free use is not a promise of an indefinitely available online service.</p><p>Accounts are free. Purchases, paid plans and self-service upgrades are currently unavailable. Signup does not charge you, enroll you in a paid subscription, or issue a licence key. Some features, such as Flow AI and Events, are planned as paid features; any paid offer will show its price, what it includes, any usage limits (such as AI credits), the billing period, any automatic renewal and how to cancel before you choose to purchase. See <a href="/download">download details</a> for current release availability and requirements.</p></section>

    <section aria-labelledby="content"><h2 id="content">4. Your recordings and files</h2><p>You retain your rights in your recordings and outputs. These terms do not transfer ownership of that content to us. You allow us and the providers that operate the Services for us to host, copy, transmit and process your content only as needed to provide the features you use (for example, an AI feature you start or a file you send to support), to keep the Services secure, and to comply with the law. You are responsible for having the permissions needed to record, edit, process and share content, including any consent required from people you record.</p><p>Flowmaster’s recording and editing tools process your files on your computer. Keep backups, allow space for originals and exports, and review exported files before removing originals. Clean sends selected files to the Windows Recycle Bin, but recovery is not guaranteed. Flowmaster is not a backup service, and we cannot restore files we do not hold.</p></section>

    <section aria-labelledby="ai"><h2 id="ai">5. AI features</h2><p>Some features use artificial intelligence. When you use a cloud AI feature, such as Flow AI or cloud transcription, the material that task needs (for example, your messages, audio, transcripts, still frames and project details) is sent through our Services to third-party AI providers, currently Anthropic and ElevenLabs, as our <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a> describes. Only submit material you have the right to submit, and do not use AI features to create unlawful, infringing, deceptive, harassing or otherwise harmful content, or in ways our AI providers’ published usage policies prohibit.</p><p>AI output, including transcripts, captions, summaries, suggested edits and detected events, may be inaccurate or incomplete. Check it before you rely on it or publish it; it is not professional advice. As between you and us, we claim no ownership of AI output produced for you from your content. AI features may require a paid plan or credits, may be limited, changed or withdrawn, and may refuse a request.</p></section>

    <section aria-labelledby="use"><h2 id="use">6. Responsible use</h2><p>Do not use the Services to violate others’ rights or applicable law, access accounts or data without authorization, distribute malicious software, disrupt the Services, send automated requests beyond normal use, or falsify account, device, trial, or licence records. Do not bypass service security, licence or trial limits, or AI credit limits. These restrictions do not limit rights that cannot lawfully be restricted, including applicable rights concerning software interoperability or third-party licensed components.</p><p>If you discover a security problem, report it to <a href={`mailto:${supportEmail}`}>{supportEmail}</a> without disclosing other users’ data or continuing activity that could cause harm.</p></section>

    <section aria-labelledby="services"><h2 id="services">7. Availability, updates, and other services</h2><p>Flowmaster may change as we fix bugs and develop features. Downloads, online checks, AI features and account services may be unavailable during outages, maintenance, provider problems or security incidents. Preview and beta features may change or be withdrawn; planned features and release dates are not guarantees.</p><p>Flowmaster works with other software and providers, including OBS Studio and optional Google sign-in. Those services have their own terms, availability, and compatibility requirements, and we are not responsible for them. Keep required components up to date and review the requirements for your installed version.</p></section>

    <section aria-labelledby="suspension"><h2 id="suspension">8. Restricting or ending access</h2><p>We may restrict accounts, devices, or access to the Services when reasonably necessary to address a material violation of these terms or the EULA, trial or licence abuse, a security risk, or a legal requirement. Where practicable, we will explain the reason and how to contact us; urgent security or legal circumstances may require action first.</p><p>If you believe a restriction or usage decision is incorrect, contact support for review. You may stop using Flowmaster at any time and request account deletion as described in our <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>. Ending online access does not transfer ownership of your local recordings to us or erase those files. The EULA continues to govern use of the installed software.</p></section>

    <section aria-labelledby="warranties"><h2 id="warranties">9. Warranties and liability</h2><p>To the extent permitted by applicable law, the website and Services, including AI features and their output, are provided “as is” and “as available,” without warranties of any kind, including implied warranties of merchantability, fitness for a particular purpose, non-infringement, accuracy or uninterrupted operation. Test your workflow and check important outputs before relying on them.</p><p>To the extent permitted by applicable law, we are not liable for indirect, incidental, special or consequential losses, including lost profits, revenue, audience or opportunities, or loss of data or files, arising from the website or Services. Our total liability for all claims relating to the website or Services will not exceed the greater of the amount you paid us in the twelve months before the event giving rise to the claim or US$50. These are the same limits as the EULA. Nothing in these terms excludes or limits liability for fraud, gross negligence, wilful misconduct, death or personal injury caused by negligence, or any liability that cannot legally be excluded or limited. Your mandatory consumer rights and remedies remain unaffected, and some limitations may not apply where you live.</p></section>

    <section aria-labelledby="privacy"><h2 id="privacy">10. Privacy and communications</h2><p>Our <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a> explains account information, Google sign-in, device and trial records, crash reports and usage statistics, AI providers, service providers, and privacy requests, including California privacy rights. We may send necessary account, security, and service messages. Creating an account is not consent to marketing emails; optional announcements require a separate opt-in.</p></section>

    <section aria-labelledby="law"><h2 id="law">11. Governing law and disputes</h2><p>These terms and any dispute arising out of or relating to them, the website or the Services are governed by the laws of the State of California, USA, without regard to its conflict-of-laws rules. Before starting a formal dispute, please contact us so we can try to resolve the issue informally. Except where the law gives you the right to bring a claim where you live, any lawsuit must be brought in the state or federal courts located in California, and you and we consent to their jurisdiction. If you are a consumer, nothing in these terms takes away the mandatory consumer protections of the place where you live.</p><p>California users: under California Civil Code Section 1789.3, you may contact the Complaint Assistance Unit of the Division of Consumer Services of the California Department of Consumer Affairs in writing at 1625 North Market Blvd., Suite N 112, Sacramento, CA 95834, or by telephone at (800) 952-5210.</p></section>

    <section aria-labelledby="updates"><h2 id="updates">12. Changes, general terms and contact</h2><p>We will publish changes here and update the date above. Material changes will receive additional notice where required, and we will seek agreement where applicable law requires it. Changes apply going forward and do not remove rights that already accrued. If any part of these terms is unenforceable, the rest remains in effect, and our failure to enforce a term is not a waiver of it. We may transfer these terms in connection with a sale or reorganization of the Flowmaster business, or to a business entity we form to operate Flowmaster, and will tell you if we do.</p><p>For questions, account issues, or a review of an access decision, contact Flowmaster (Alexander Blair, doing business as Flowmaster) at <a href={`mailto:${supportEmail}`}>{supportEmail}</a>. Include enough detail to identify the issue, but never send your password, sign-in codes, or API keys.</p></section>

    <div class="terms-bottom"><a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy →</a><a href="/account">Your Flowmaster account →</a><a href="/download">Download details →</a></div>
